i</surname><given-names>AX</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>XT</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>XQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A standardized method to propagate <italic>Cryptocaryon irritans</italic> on a susceptible host pompano <italic>Trachinotus ovatus</italic></article-title><source>Aquaculture</source><year>2006</year><volume>258</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>133</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.aquaculture.2006.04.026</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Dan XM, Li AX, Lin XT, Zhu XQ (2006) A standardized method to propagate Cryptocaryon irritans on a susceptible host pompano Trachinotus ovatus. Aquaculture 258:127&#x02013;133 </citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diggles</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Some information on the morphology of <italic>Cryptocaryon irritans</italic> from South-East Queensland, Australia</article-title><source>Europ J Protistol</source><year>1997</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>200</fpage><lpage>210</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Diggles BK (1997) Some information on the morphology of Cryptocaryon irritans from South-East Queensland, Australia. Europ J Protistol 33:200&#x02013;210 </citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diggles</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lester</surname><given-names>RJG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of temperature and host species on the development of <italic>Cryptocaryon irritans</italic></article-title><source>J Parasitol</source><year>1996</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3284114</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-uns